    "note": "PROVEME — the prediction made before the build held exactly: `cairnmap --gate` dropped from 21 findings to 6, and the 6 are name-for-name the ones the ticket put out of bounds (/ruled chartered-but-not-installed, five bin/cmd entries no charter's invoke names). 20/20 teeth green twice; edges 9/9 twice. skill_roster() is now skill_membership(), deriving from the node class's own `members_derived_by` rule and naming THREE faults, each exactly one red: no rule declared (the ABSENT-KEY shape `.get(key, [])` swallowed), `members_so_far` back, or a rule that stops naming skills/. `every_chartered_skill_is_on_the_roster` is RETIRED with a note naming its successor — under derivation it compares a set against a superset of itself, a green arithmetic guarantees, which Law 8 calls worse here than a red. Its falsifiable half survives as `every_skill_directory_carries_a_charter`. THREE BUGS THE VOYAGE UNCOVERED AND FIXED (bounds ruling 2026-09-09): (1) the proof's lane floor was `len(record) >= 8`, a count that cannot say WHICH lane went missing — now the lanes are named, so retiring one is an edit to that list; (2) TEETH was collected at import time, so a tooth appended at the end of the file never ran and the file printed a confident 19/19 over it — now collected at call time; (3) the WATCHME probe's first reading counted the gate's ABSOLUTE red total and fired at 7, six of which were the corpus's standing out-of-bounds findings — rewritten to read the DELTA a substituted starved node class adds, which is the only attributable number.",
